        "example": "Urgency: Nokia CEO Stephen Elop's 'burning platform' memo. 'We are standing on a burning platform.' Created urgency that enabled massive change (partnership with Microsoft). Too little, too late — but the urgency creation was powerful. | Short-Term Wins: large ERP implementation (24 months). Month 3: automate one department's reporting (saves 5 hours/week). Celebrate. People see progress. Momentum builds. Don't wait 12 months for a win — create wins every 30-60 days. | Institute Change: after successful transformation, don't declare victory. Kotter: 70% of transformations fail in the last phase — leaders move on too quickly. Embed new behaviors in performance reviews, hiring criteria, and promotion decisions. Culture = 'the way we do things here.'",
