        "name": "Crisis First Hour",
        "definition": "Activate team, confirm containment, preserve evidence, draft holding statement, notify board. Speed + accuracy + empathy.",
        "formula": null,
        "example": "Tylenol 1982: 7 deaths from cyanide-laced capsules. Johnson & Johnson recalled 31M bottles within days. Became gold standard for crisis response. | Equifax 2017: 147M records breached. Took 6 weeks to notify. CEO and CIO resigned. $700M settlement. Speed matters. | Buffer 2013: Hacked, spammed users. CEO posted real-time updates on blog every 30 min. No customers left. Transparency saved them.",
