        "formula": null,
        "example": "Exploit: Quarterly targets, efficiency metrics, Six Sigma, cost reduction. Run by operational managers. | Explore: Long time horizons, tolerate failure, small autonomous teams, venture-style funding. Run by entrepreneurial leaders. | Amazon: Exploit = retail operations (fulfillment optimization, pricing algorithms). Explore = AWS (started as internal tool, now $90B). Bezos kept AWS separate from retail — different culture, different metrics. | Failure mode: Using exploit metrics on explore teams kills innovation ('this R&D project has no ROI after 6 months').",
