        "name": "Pareto Principle (80/20)",
        "definition": "80% of effects come from 20% of causes. Applied to operations: 80% of quality issues from 20% of defect types, 80% of revenue from 20% of customers, 80% of delays from 20% of process steps. Focus on the vital 20%.",
        "formula": null,
        "example": "Quality: 80% of customer complaints caused by 3 out of 50 product defects. Fix those 3 first. | Revenue: 80% of revenue from 20% of customers. Give those 20% white-glove treatment. | Inventory: 80% of inventory value in 20% of SKUs. Optimize those first. | Time management: 80% of results from 20% of activities. Identify and protect that 20%. Delegate or eliminate the rest. | Pareto chart: Bar chart sorted by frequency + cumulative % line. Visually identifies the vital few vs trivial many.",
