        "name": "RACI Mapping",
        "definition": "For every decision or deliverable, assign: Responsible (does the work), Accountable (approves — only ONE), Consulted (input before decision), Informed (told after decision). Clarifies who owns what.",
        "formula": null,
        "example": "Product launch: R = Product Manager (does work). A = VP Product (one approver). C = Engineering lead, Sales lead, Legal (consulted beforehand). I = CEO, Board, All-hands (informed afterward). | Mistake: having multiple As (two 'approvers' means no one is truly accountable). | Mistake: not Consulting Legal before a regulatory decision. The 'CC' trap — forward-thinking RACI mapping prevents this.",
