        "name": "Leading Churn Indicators",
        "definition": "Don't wait for churn. Identify behavioral patterns that PREDICT churn: declining usage, fewer support tickets (given up), downgrade activity. Act before they leave.",
        "formula": null,
        "example": "Cohort A: average 15 logins/week in Month 1. Cohort B: average 8 logins/week in Month 1. Cohort B WILL churn more. Early engagement predicts retention. | Leading indicators: login frequency, feature adoption, support ticket type (is it 'how do I?' or 'I want to cancel?'), NPS drop. | Build a churn prediction model: if a customer has <5 logins in Week 2 and hasn't used a core feature, trigger a CSM intervention. Proactive > reactive.",
