        "example": "Time cohort: 'Users who signed up in January 2025.' Track their retention over 12 months. Compare to February 2025 cohort. | Behavior cohort: 'Users whose first purchase was Product X.' Do they retain differently from users who started with Product Y? | Combined: 'January cohort, Product X starters.' Now you know: time effect, product effect, AND interaction. January cohort with Product X has 80% retention — but February cohort with Product X has 50%. Something changed in February.",
