        "example": "Bad reasoning: 'We chose Vendor A because they have a great reputation.' Good: 'Vendor A scored highest on our weighted criteria: cost (30%), quality (30%), reliability (25%), culture fit (15%). Their reference checks scored 9.2/10 vs vendor B's 7.1. Sensitivity analysis shows the decision holds even if we halve the weight on cost.' | Decision tree: map the reasoning visually — at each chance node, what's the probability? At each decision node, what's the EV? The tree IS the reasoning.",
