        "formula": null,
        "example": "DQF audit: 'We have 3 years of customer churn data (high reliability). We have 0 data on competitor response to our pricing change (low reliability, high sensitivity).' Action: commission competitive intelligence before deciding. | Information quality spectrum: Proven facts > Expert judgment > Educated guesses > Wild assumptions. Label each input in your model. | Value of information question: 'If we spent $50k and 2 weeks getting better data on X, would our decision change?' If no, stop researching X.",
