        "name": "Combining Intuition + Analysis",
        "definition": "The best decisions use BOTH: 1) Analysis to generate options and eliminate clearly bad ones 2) Intuition to select between the remaining viable options 3) Analysis again to stress-test the intuitive choice.",
        "formula": null,
        "example": "Vendor selection: Analysis: score 10 vendors on weighted criteria. Narrow to top 3. Intuition: meet each top vendor's team. Which one 'feels' like a partner? Select. Analysis: run sensitivity analysis. 'If we overweight cost, does the choice change?' If not, confident decision. | Jeff Bezos: 'If you can make the decision with analysis, make it. If you can't, use intuition — but know that's what you're doing.' The key is AWARENESS of which mode you're in. | When analysis and intuition conflict: DON'T override analysis with gut unless you can articulate WHY the analysis missed something.",
