        "formula": null,
        "example": "NIST CSF maturity model: Tier 1 (Partial) — ad-hoc, reactive. Tier 2 (Risk-Informed) — management approved, not organization-wide. Tier 3 (Repeatable) — formal policy, regularly updated. Tier 4 (Adaptive) — continuous improvement, lessons learned from incidents, external threat intelligence integration. | Board reporting: 'We're at NIST Tier 2, targeting Tier 3 within 12 months.' Clear, benchmarked, credible. | Adoption: US federal agencies are mandated to use NIST CSF. Private sector adoption is increasing as boards expect structured cyber governance.",
