        "id": "16ad05f9-7cc8-43d6-86d5-41123dfe80bd",
        "name": "Supply Chain Geopolitical Mapping",
        "definition": "Map every Tier 1-2 supplier by country and sub-region. Identify geographic concentration: 'We have 3 suppliers — all in Taiwan.' Overlay with geopolitical risk: China-Taiwan tensions, South China Sea shipping lanes, semiconductor foundry concentration.",
        "formula": null,
        "example": "Semiconductor supply chain mapping: design (US, UK, Israel), fabrication (Taiwan 63%, South Korea 18%, China 6%), packaging (Taiwan, China, Malaysia). Any disruption in the Taiwan Strait → 63% of advanced chip production stops. Mitigate: TSMC building fabs in Arizona, Japan, and Germany (diversification). | Apparel supply chain: Vietnam 40%, Bangladesh 30%, China 30%. Map exposed to climate (Bangladesh floods), labor (Vietnam minimum wage increases), logistics (Suez Canal for EU shipments from Asia). | Strategy: no single country >30% of supply for critical components.",
